>
> I was hoping you would be able to help me. I defined a simmer process with the sequence of 7 required stations to produce one product. I ran the simulation and I found out that I would be producing 150 units per hour. Next, I wanted to use the simmer.optim function to determine the number of  stations needed in order to produce 1500 units per hour but this is my only constraint. How could I get the simmer.optim to work in this situation? Could you please advise?

That's not a constraint, but an objective. There must be some
constraints. Otherwise, there are potentially infinite ways of getting
that number.

Iñaki

